==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{confix|dys|pepsin|ia|lang=en}}

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/dɪsˈpɛp.si.ə/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# {{lb|en|pathology}} Any [[mild]] [[disorder]] of [[digestion]], characterised by [[stomach]] pain, discomfort, [[heartburn]] and [[nausea]], often following a meal.
#* ''He divides '''dyspepsias''' into accidental, temporary (indigestions) and habitual.''
#* {{RQ:Wodehouse Offing|XII|I've never hunted myself, but I understand that half the battle is being able to make noises like some jungle animal with '''dyspepsia''', and I believe that Aunt Dahlia in her prime could lift fellow-members of the Quorn and Pytchley out of their saddles with a single yip, though separated from them by two ploughed fields and a spinney.}}

